WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.333
Quick recap: three repair jobs.

00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:05.282
During copying, DNA polymerase proofreads.

00:00:05.909 --> 00:00:07.824
It fixes its own mistake right away.

00:00:08.451 --> 00:00:11.388
After copying, mismatch repair proteins find wrong

00:00:11.458 --> 00:00:13.188
bases in the finished DNA.

00:00:13.815 --> 00:00:15.336
And UV damage gets cut out and

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:15.940
replaced.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.308
Think of fixing typos as you go,

00:00:18.355 --> 00:00:19.527
then checking at the end.

00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:23.300
Proofreading fixes errors during copying, mismatch repair

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.437
fixes them after, and UV damage is

00:00:25.495 --> 00:00:26.563
cut out and replaced.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.525
Let's see what you remember.
